## 🌐 MCP SERVERS

You have access to the following MCP servers as specified in `.roo/HOW-IT-WORKS.md`:

### context7 (`npx -y @upstash/context7-mcp@latest`)
Provides tools to resolve library IDs and fetch documentation. Useful if the bug seems related to misunderstanding or misuse of a specific library/framework API.
- `resolve-library-id`: Get Context7 ID for a library name.
- `get-library-docs`: Fetch documentation using a Context7 ID.

### repomix (`npx -y repomix --mcp`)
Provides tools to package local or remote codebases for analysis. Can be useful for understanding the broader context of the code where the bug occurs, especially in complex codebases.
- `pack_codebase`: Package local directory.
- `pack_remote_repository`: Package GitHub repository.
- `read_repomix_output`: Read output file (for restricted environments).
- `file_system_read_file`: Read file via absolute path.
- `file_system_read_directory`: List directory via absolute path.

### tavily (`npx -y tavily-mcp@latest`)
Provides tools for web search and content extraction. Extremely useful for searching for specific error messages, finding solutions to known issues, or looking up debugging techniques for particular technologies.
- `tavily-search`: Perform AI-powered web search.
- `tavily-extract`: Extract content from URLs found during search.


### browser-tools-mcp (`/Users/andreyvavilov/.nvm/versions/node/v22.6.0/bin/browser-tools-mcp `)
Provides tools for interacting with and inspecting a web browser instance. Useful for debugging web applications by checking logs, errors, or taking screenshots.
- `getConsoleLogs`: Check browser console logs.
- `getConsoleErrors`: Check browser console errors.
- `getNetworkErrors`: Check network ERROR logs.
- `getNetworkLogs`: Check ALL network logs.
- `takeScreenshot`: Take a screenshot of the current browser tab.
- `getSelectedElement`: Get the selected element from the browser.
- `wipeLogs`: Wipe all browser logs from memory.
- `runAccessibilityAudit`: Run an accessibility audit on the current page.
- `runPerformanceAudit`: Run a performance audit on the current page.
- `runSEOAudit`: Run an SEO audit on the current page.
- `runNextJSAudit`: Run a Next.js audit.
- `runDebuggerMode`: Run debugger mode.
- `runAuditMode`: Run audit mode.
- `runBestPracticesAudit`: Run a best practices audit.
